  When searching for a secret door that I *know* is there I use
"n11s" to search eleven times in a row.  Sometimes I have to do
it three times before I find the door.  That's at least 23 
searches to find it (as a wizard.)

  Force bolt is a nice secret door finder, but I'd try the walls
I've marked with "Here" first.  Just use mix in an occasional 
force bolt with your searching so you don't run yourself 
completely out of Power.  

  NB.  Each search command checks the surrounding eight squares.
So move three squares along after each extended search.

  Don't forget the bottom wall of the bottom right (and possibly 
bottom middle) rooms, depending on how close they are to the edge
of the map.  Ditto for the top wall of the top room.


  The right-hand corridor (that I've marked with asterisks) also 
looks like a good place to search for a hidden corridor.  I don't
know if force bolt will find hidden corridors.  I usually search 
corridors by doing move, search, move, search, etc.  Each wall of
the corridor gets searched three times.  (It's a nice frenetic 
activity to take off some of the frustration.)


  If that trap in the upper room is a hole or trap door, you 
could jump into it and come back up.


  Or you could use Force bolt on the back to back boulders 
blocking you from the mines.


